<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="no"?>
<!-- ===========================================================================
     Animal Redux, ENGLISH. This is the reference file: every other language is
     a copy of it with the text attributes translated.

     ADDING A LANGUAGE
       Copy this file to translation_<code>.xml (translation_de.xml,
       translation_fr.xml, ...) and translate ONLY the text attributes. Leave
       every name attribute exactly as it is: those are keys, not words.
       PARTIAL TRANSLATIONS ARE WELCOME AND SAFE. Any key you leave out falls
       back to the English shipped in the code, so a half-finished file never
       breaks the mod and never shows a raw key on screen.

     TWO RULES THAT WILL BITE YOU
       1. An XML comment may not contain a double hyphen ANYWHERE. It is a parse
          error and the whole file silently fails to load, taking every string
          with it. Note the asymmetry: a double hyphen inside a text attribute
          is perfectly legal, so the file may well contain them.
       2. Overrun text is CLIPPED, not wrapped. Table columns and the footer
          button bar are fixed width, so a translation longer than its budget
          is silently cut off mid-word. German runs roughly 30 percent longer
          than English. Character budgets are noted per block below.

     KEY NAMING, so a key can be found from what it does
       ar_ui_*      page titles, tab names, section headings
       ar_col_*     table column headers      (TIGHT: budget noted per column)
       ar_btn_*     buttons                   (TIGHT: the footer bar is shared)
       ar_set_*     settings. Convention, NOT a parallel list:
                      ar_set_<id>        the row title
                      ar_set_<id>_tt     its tooltip
                      ar_set_<id>_v<N>   value label N, counting from 1
                    Resolving by convention rather than an array means the
                    labels cannot drift out of step with the values, which
                    matters because the SAVE FILE AND THE NETWORK CARRY THE
                    INDEX, never the label. A mislabel is a player choosing one
                    thing while the screen says another.
       ar_msg_*     in game messages and notifications
       ar_status_*  status words shown in a cell
       ar_food_*    feed and ration vocabulary
       ar_rule_*    auto sell rule vocabulary

     WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE
       Log output. A player pasting log.txt into a bug report needs it in
       English, and so do we. Internal enum values and anything compared against
       a literal are likewise never translated: they are keys wearing the
       costume of words.
     =========================================================================== -->
<l10n>
    <texts>
